title: 'HRMP: widen the accepted origins and let paras make a few free requests'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    In Polkadot HRMP, in preparation for AHMv2:

    - Widen the accepted origins of `establish_system_channel` and `poke_channel_deposits`.
    - Expose `max_para_request_weight`, the weight of the heaviest request a parachain makes for
      itself.
    - Bound how many requests a non-system parachain makes: `MaxRequestsPerWindow` per window
      of `RequestWindow` blocks. Requests involves sending XCMs which is a limited resource,
      and we don't want to charge parachains, so a throttling mechanism is chosen.

    In `xcm-builder`: add the barrier `AllowUnpaidTransactFrom`, which lets an origin have one
    call dispatched as itself without paying, under a weight bound, and the filter
    `IsChildNonSystemParachain`.

    Westend uses them to execute, for free, a call of a non-system parachain that weighs no more
    than an HRMP request, and allows 10 requests per day to each of them.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: pallet-hrmp-relay
  bump: patch
- name: staging-xcm-builder
  bump: minor
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-test-runtime
  bump: patch
